  "S3": {
    "bottom_line_reference": "On the oracle assumption set, discounting unlevered FCFF at a market-built WACC of 12.62% yields an enterprise value of ~$2.17tn. Adjusting for NVIDIA's large net-cash position (net debt of -$54.1bn) and $22.3bn of non-marketable equity securities gives equity value of ~$2.25tn, or roughly $92 per diluted share. That is under half the ~$207 market price, implying material overvaluation on these inputs. However, this depends entirely on the assumed 5-year growth taper, margins, cash tax rate and terminal growth, none of which come from the filing. Terminal value is ~70% of EV, so the answer is sensitive to the WACC-g spread; a +-50bp WACC move shifts value ~12%. The 10-K itself discloses no WACC, so any claim about a 'company published WACC' is unfounded. A trading-multiple and capex-normalization cross-check is warranted before acting.",
    "assumption_conditional": true,
